selectedTimeline.body:
This could cause confusing behavior if the original Promise rejects with a non-error:

```js
function promiseFunction() {
  return Promise.reject(null);
}

util.callbackify(promiseFunction)((err, result) => {
  // err will be null, which could be confusing because the promise actually rejected.
});
```

Bluebird seems to handle this by [wrapping the rejection reason in an `Error` if it's falsy](https://github.com/petkaantonov/bluebird/blob/2207fae3572f03b089bc92d3a6cefdd278cff7ab/src/nodeify.js#L30-L43).

